.TH OMACHAT 1 "2026-10-28" "OmaChat"
.SH NAME
omachat \- terminal client for Nostr direct messages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omachat
[--socket PATH]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Connects to the local
.B omachatd
socket and opens a conversation window.
The first connection calls chat-prepare, which seals a nostr-identity-v1 key
when none is stored.
The npub is shown in the sidebar.
This program never prints an nsec.
.SH COMMANDS
/help, /npub, /prepare,
/contact add PEER, /contact remove NPUB, /contacts, /open PEER,
/relays, /relays set URL...,
/handle claim NAME, /handle bind, /handle unbind,
/panic ERASE, /quit.
PEER is an npub, a 64-character public key, or name@domain.
A line that is not a slash command sends to the selected contact.
.SH FILES
Default socket: $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/omachat/omachat.sock.
.SH SEE ALSO
omachatd(8), omachat-ctl(1), omachat-protocol(7)
